WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.710
Speaking of embarrassment and shame, a new
poll confirms what should obviously be the

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:07.930
case.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:13.940
And yet in America, when 60 million people
voted for Donald Trump, it would be wrong

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:17.560
to assume that what makes sense will be.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:24.349
Most Americans are embarrassed, however, by
the Trump corona virus response, according

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:26.820
to a new SSR poll.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:32.930
So not only are we the laughing stock of the
world and the pity of the world, we are also

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:34.320
embarrassed.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.320
Which is good.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:40.270
We should be the right emotion is to be embarrassed
by what we've done on this planet.

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:45.760
As far as coronavirus is concerned, so a few
notes from this poll, disapproval of Trump's

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.220
handling of the virus is up to 58 percent.

00:00:49.220 --> 00:00:50.220
Great.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.220
But how does 42 percent of the country think
Trump did a good job on the virus?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.220
That's a problem.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:59.350
Eight in 10 Americans are angry about the
response.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.070
And 51 percent are very angry.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:05.689
Well, people should be angry, but that's deceptive
because some people are angry because of how

00:01:05.689 --> 00:01:07.270
bad the response has been.

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:10.530
While some people are angry that they have
to wear masks, so that one is a little bit

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.930
less clear.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:17.460
But then the headline, seven in 10 Americans
are embarrassed by the response.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:20.350
And we should be embarrassed because it's
been embarrassing.

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:27.609
And now there are also two important indicators
in this poll about when things should start

00:01:27.609 --> 00:01:28.899
to return to normal.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:34.799
Now, 57 percent of Americans say schools should
not open for in-person classes in the fall.

00:01:34.799 --> 00:01:36.429
Some have already opened.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:38.460
But that's not a huge majority anyway.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:44.950
Only 57 percent say keep schools closed in
the fall for in-person do remote for sports.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:49.350
Forty nine percent of Americans say there
should not be in person sports.

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.240
Forty five percent of Americans say there
should be in person sports.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.579
These are really depressing numbers.

00:01:56.579 --> 00:02:03.329
Even with this polarized country, you would
think you would hope that almost everyone

00:02:03.329 --> 00:02:05.840
would realize, guys, this is embarrassing.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.819
Obviously, we're not in a position to open
schools right now.

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:10.780
It's not about never open them.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:15.270
It's about let's just do remote for one more
semester and then hopefully we'll have a vaccine

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:19.260
and better treatments and things can start
to normalize in early 2021.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.099
No embarrassing schools shouldn't yet open.

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:27.950
But that's not what most people or what nearly
half of Americans believe.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:32.650
Now, don't forget, when you look at these
numbers, we talked about this yesterday on

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:33.870
the show.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:38.780
Somewhere between 40 and 50 percent of this
country doesn't even plan to get the vaccine,

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:43.659
which will make herd immunity impossible in
any kind of short to medium term.

00:02:43.659 --> 00:02:47.680
So the real headlines here are reversed, right?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:48.700
Instead of.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:53.300
Wow, 70 percent of Americans embarrassed by
Trump's coronavirus response.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.410
The red alert is whoa.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:03:00.120
Thirty percent of Americans aren't embarrassed
by Trump's corona virus response.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.099
That's where the focus should be.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:04.150
That's about 100 million people.

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.860
If you include, you know, out of the full
population, which includes kids, but fine

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.770
with adults, it would be some smaller number
than that.

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:16.439
20 percent of Americans aren't angry about
Trump's coronavirus response.

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:17.439
What?

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:18.750
That's like 60 million people.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:19.750
Oh, wait.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:21.959
Trump got about 60 million votes in 2016.

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:28.310
Now, if we go back to embarrassment for a
second, yeah, we should be embarrassed about

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.799
Trump's response to coronavirus.

00:03:30.799 --> 00:03:32.260
And I am.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:37.010
But we should be just as embarrassed by the
reactions and the behavior of a huge portion

00:03:37.010 --> 00:03:38.590
of the country's people.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:43.049
I've said before, when Trump leaves, we still
have 60 million Trump ists to deal with.

00:03:43.049 --> 00:03:46.129
We've seen protests against mass squaring.

00:03:46.129 --> 00:03:49.620
We've seen protests against social distancing
guidelines.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:56.959
We've seen people losing their minds in Costco's
and Wal-Mart's about liberty and freedom over

00:03:56.959 --> 00:04:00.700
wearing a mask and trying to stop the spread
of a virus.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:07.189
Conspiracy theories about Dr. Anthony Foushee
to the point where he needs security and his

00:04:07.189 --> 00:04:08.550
daughters need security.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:11.340
Bill Gates wants to microchip you.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:17.700
It is embarrassing what Trump has done, but
it's doubly embarrassing when we look not

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:23.440
at Trump himself, but at his administration's
response at the people around him.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.289
And at our fellow Americans.

00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:29.290
At some point we're going to be past this
and we'll be able to do a postmortem.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:35.530
And we will need to include in our analysis,
not just an analysis of what Trump did and

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:40.580
didn't do, not just an analysis of what the
Trump administration didn't didn't do.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:46.560
But we're going to need to do an analysis
of the 60 million people who voted once for

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.310
this guy and are going to vote for him a second
time.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:53.070
Hopefully, it won't be enough to give him
another four years.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:56.840
And we have to contend with them for a very
long time.

00:04:56.840 --> 00:04:59.100
And I've not gotten any good answers to this.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.210
I've now talked about this for a couple of
weeks.

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:07.180
And the main point is if Trump wins, he's
going to do it with sixty five, 66, 67 million

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:08.180
voters.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:14.020
If Trump loses, he's going to lose with 60
to 63 million voters, maybe even 64 million

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.050
voters.

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:18.770
Even if he loses, we have 60 something million
Trump ists in this country.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.300
They're on school boards.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:22.680
They are working in stores that you go to.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:26.570
They are maybe your family, they're maybe
your relatives, your friends, whatever.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.500
What do we do about that?

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:34.870
Because we as a country are not really going
to be able to advance until we do something

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:39.190
to weed out the ideology that got 60 million
plus people to vote for Trump.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.240
Not once, but no doubt.

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:45.550
Twice or we have to figure out a way to make
progress around them.

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:46.759
Or despite them.

00:05:46.759 --> 00:05:48.250
And I don't know what the answer is.

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.550
I'm always open to hearing ideas from you.

